{"duration_api_ms":17792,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dcf4e349-fc2d-4a99-ac16-870d6ce868d5","total_cost_usd":0.07086780000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2416,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":2562,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2562,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":2562,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2416,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.07086780000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the two planetary encounters before being directed to Uranus.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Although Voyager 2 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the two planetary encounters\"},{\"text\":\"Mission planners directed Voyager 2 to Uranus.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus\"},{\"text\":\"The journey of Voyager 2 to Uranus would take about 4,5 years.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"a journey that would take about 4,5 years\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2's encounter with Saturn was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"In fact, its encounter with Saturn was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\"},{\"text\":\"The geometry of Voyager 2's Uranus encounter was defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"The Uranus encounter’s geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 had only 5.5 hours of close study during its Uranus flyby.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Voyager 2 had only 5.5 hours of close study during its flyby.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 was the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 began its long-range observations of Uranus on Nov. 4, 1985.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Voyager 2 began its long-range observations of the planet on Nov. 4, 1985\"},{\"text\":\"On Nov. 4, 1985, signals from Voyager 2 took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\"},{\"text\":\"Light conditions at Uranus were 400 times less than terrestrial conditions.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Light conditions were 400 times less than terrestrial conditions.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2's closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 UTC Jan. 24, 1986.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 UTC Jan. 24, 1986\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2's closest approach to Uranus was at a range of about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers).\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"at a range of about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\"},{\"text\":\"During its Uranus flyby, Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered 10 new moons\"},{\"text\":\"The new moons of Uranus discovered by Voyager 2 were given names such as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"given such names as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\"},{\"text\":\"The names of the new Uranian moons discovered by Voyager 2 are allusions to Shakespeare.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"obvious allusions to Shakespeare\"},{\"text\":\"The Shakespearean naming tradition for Uranus' moons began with Titania and Oberon.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"continuing a naming tradition that began with Titania and Oberon\"},{\"text\":\"Titania and Oberon were discovered in 1787.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"discovered in 1787\"},{\"text\":\"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered two new rings of Uranus.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"two new rings in addition to the “older” nine rings\"},{\"text\":\"Uranus had nine previously known rings before Voyager 2's flyby.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"two new rings in addition to the “older” nine rings\"},{\"text\":\"During its flyby, Voyager 2 discovered a magnetic field of Uranus tilted at about 59 degrees off-axis.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"a magnetic field tilted at about 59 degrees off-axis and off-center\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 found that Uranus' magnetic field is off-center.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"a magnetic field tilted at about 59 degrees off-axis and off-center\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 found wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 miles per hour (724 kilometers per hour).\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"The spacecraft found wind speeds in Uranus’ atmosphere as high as 450 miles per hour (724 kilometers per hour)\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 found evidence of a boiling ocean of water some 497 miles (800 kilometers) below the top cloud surface of Uranus.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"found evidence of a boiling ocean of water some 497 miles (800 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"},{\"text\":\"Uranus' rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency.\"},{\"text\":\"Uranus' rings were found to be extremely variable in transparency.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 returned photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Voyager 2 also returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania\"},{\"text\":\"Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, Umbriel, and Titania are five of Uranus' larger moons.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"five of Uranus’ larger moons\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2 flew by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers).\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\"},{\"text\":\"In flying by Miranda, Voyager 2 came closest to any object so far in its travels.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 2's travels had lasted nearly a decade at the time of the Miranda flyby.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly decade-long travels\"},{\"text\":\"Images of Miranda showed a surface that was a mishmash of peculiar features.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Images of the moon showed a strange object whose surface was a mishmash of peculiar features that seemed to have no rhyme or reason.\"},{\"text\":\"Uranus appeared generally featureless in Voyager 2 images.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless.\"},{\"text\":\"The news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the Challenger accident.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The spectacular news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the tragic Challenger accident\"},{\"text\":\"The Challenger accident killed seven astronauts.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"killed seven astronauts\"},{\"text\":\"The Challenger accident occurred during the space shuttle launch on Jan. 28, 1986.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"during their space shuttle launch Jan. 28, 1986\"}]}","ttft_ms":22297,"type":"result","duration_ms":22314,"uuid":"3b7d7b66-bb9f-43b0-a631-d998e46a7e96","ttft_stream_ms":5905,"time_to_request_ms":4520,"first_content_frame_ms":5906,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
